@meta
id: 28-04
title: Drill — one line, one reason
chapter: 28
type: drill
skills: vimrc-structure
par: 82
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: nothing — settings.json has no room for why
open: .vimrc

@brief
Eight times: add `set scrolloff=5` to the end of the Looks section, with
the reason written beside it, and save.

    set scrolloff=5           " keep 5 lines visible above and below

The reason is the point of the drill. A bare option name is a thing you
will Google again in a year; the line above tells you, in the half
second you have while scrolling past, why you wanted it.

@keys
| `G` | last line |
| `o` | open a line below |
| `:wq` | save and quit |

@hints
The section only has three lines, so `G` and `o` is the whole route.
--
Type the setting, then spaces, then `"` and the reason. Everything after
an unmatched `"` on a vimrc line is a comment.

@solution
    G o set scrolloff=5           " keep 5 lines visible above and below <Esc> :wq<Enter>

`scrolloff` is the single most common first addition to a vimrc, and a
good example of the rule this chapter keeps repeating: you add it the
day you notice you keep pressing `zz` after every search, not the day
you read someone's dotfiles.

One caution about comments in a vimrc, since you are now writing them.
An inline `"` comment is illegal after a few commands — `:map`, `:normal`
and `:execute` among them — because they treat the quote as part of their
argument. `nnoremap <leader>w :w<CR>   " save` looks fine and silently
maps a `w` that types a stray comment. Put the comment on its own line
above the mapping instead. That trap is one of the four bugs waiting for
you at the end of this chapter.

@start .vimrc
" ~/.vimrc - one line at a time, when something annoys you.

set nocompatible
syntax on
filetype plugin indent on

" --- Looks ---
set number
set ruler
set showcmd

@expected .vimrc
" ~/.vimrc - one line at a time, when something annoys you.

set nocompatible
syntax on
filetype plugin indent on

" --- Looks ---
set number
set ruler
set showcmd
set scrolloff=5           " keep 5 lines visible above and below
